//// rakun — Spring-style application framework: future/abstract surface.
////
//// Nothing is declared here any more, and that is the point.
////
//// This file used to carry a declaration-only `behavior Context` — the intended
//// shape of a future `ctx.resolve<T>()` API, marked "not yet implemented".
//// Front 06 implemented it as a CONCRETE `pub type Context` in `src/context.bp`
//// (with `resolve` / `resolveNamed` / `has` / `beanNames` / `child` / `publish`,
//// and `__rkMake_Context()` so a field of it wires by type), so the stub had to
//// go: `rakun.d.bp` is loaded for consumers through `botopink.json`'s `files`
//// list, and leaving it would have put TWO `Context` declarations into every
//// consumer's namespace.
////
//// The file stays in `files` and keeps its place in the list. It is the
//// library's declaration module, and the next boundary interface that needs one
//// belongs here rather than in a new file.
////
//// The runtime-boundary `Request` interface moved to the real, compiled `http.bp`
//// (so handlers get its `?string` return types); the bootstrap `Rakun` is now a
//// CONCRETE record in `bootstrap.bp`. The concrete value types (`HttpMethod`/
//// `Response`/`App`) live in `http.bp`; the `#[decorator]` bodies in
//// `decorators.bp`; the host seams in `runtime.bp`.
////
//// Opt-in, never auto-loaded into the type `Env`: reached via `from "rakun"`.
//// See ./AGENTS.md, ./docs.md and the spec: tasks/v0.beta.7/specs/rakun.md
////
//// Naming note: `get`/`set`/`new` are reserved keyword tokens, so the route
//// decorators follow Spring's own names (`getMapping`, …) and the container
//// uses `resolve<T>()` rather than `get<T>()`.
